    {
      "id": "bool-3c7383",
      "name": "bool",
      "category": "AxisAngleGizmo",
      "signature": "bool(Target, Should Use Custom Destination Func)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UAxisAngleGizmo*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Should Use Custom Destination Func",
          "type": ")>",
          "default": "[]("
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TUniqueFunction<",
      "docs": "This gets checked to see if we should use the custom ray caster to get a destination point for the gizmo, rather\nthan grabbing the intersection with the gizmo plane."
    },
    {
      "id": "bool-7b0171",
      "name": "bool",
      "category": "AxisAngleGizmo",
      "signature": "bool(Target, World Ray, Custom Destination Func)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UAxisAngleGizmo*"
        },
        {
          "name": "World Ray",
          "type": "FCustomDestinationParams&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Custom Destination Func",
          "type": "FVector& OutputPoint )>",
          "default": "[](const FCustomDestinationParams& Params, FVector& OutputPoint"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TUniqueFunction<",
      "docs": "If ShouldUseCustomDestinationFunc() returns true, this function is used to get a destination point, and\nthe output parameter is picked in such a way that the closest axis in the plane of the gizmo (the positive or\nnegative x or y, if we're rotating around z, for instance) moves to the closest point in the plane to the\ndestination point.\nUsed, for instance, for aligning to items in the scene."
    },
